# Product boundary

shippin.tech is the open product and the brand. shippin.cloud is later paid hosting of the same server, not a second mail engine.

This repository is the Rust mail and groupware engine: SMTP, IMAP, JMAP, POP3, ManageSieve, CalDAV, and CardDAV.

## Current work

Make the scale image a deployable multi-tenant product. `Dockerfile.fdb`, started from `resources/scale`, runs two nodes on FoundationDB, one S3 bucket, and NATS. Two tenants share that deployment. A mailbox written for one tenant on the first node is read for that same tenant on the second node, and the other tenant cannot read it. The same process serves JMAP, CalDAV, and CardDAV so another product can connect. shippin.cloud later hosts that same image. The license choice is written only after that.

The engine already has this groundwork in `crates/common/src/auth/mod.rs`: a tenant has roles, quotas, and permissions; a domain and an account each carry `id_tenant`.

The scale compose file sets `shippin.tech_SCALE_S3_ENDPOINT`, `shippin.tech_SCALE_S3_ACCESS_KEY`, `shippin.tech_SCALE_S3_SECRET_KEY`, and `shippin.tech_SCALE_NATS_ADDRESS`. On first boot the scale binary writes those into the existing BlobStore and Coordinator registry singletons when they are empty. A one-node build without those variables does not write them.

Do not add, in this phase:

- a license choice in `Cargo.toml` or a `LICENSE` file
- shippin.cloud hosting
- a webmail, calendar, or contacts client
- a document, spreadsheet, or slide editor
- chat, meetings, or a drive product
- an admin UI
- a Go control plane
- a second mail server, including Mox, Postfix, or Dovecot

Mox is a product reference only. Do not port it or run it beside this server.

## Suite map

These capabilities were not written in this repo. Sources: [Zoho Workplace](https://www.zoho.com/workplace/) and its [edition list](https://www.zoho.com/workplace/pricing.html), the [Zoho API directory](https://www.zoho.com/developer/rest-apis/api-directory.html), and [Google Workspace developer products](https://developers.google.com/workspace/products).

This engine already covers the mail, calendar, contacts, and directory row. Other products connect to those surfaces. They are not a second mail server and they are not built inside this phase.

| Suite capability | Zoho | Google | This repository |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Mail | Mail | Gmail | SMTP, IMAP, JMAP, POP3, ManageSieve |
| Calendar | Calendar | Calendar | CalDAV |
| Contacts | Contacts, Card Scanner | People API | CardDAV |
| Tenants, domains, users, quotas | Directory, Mail Admin | Admin SDK Directory API | `TenantCache`, domains, accounts, SCIM flag, OAuth |
| Files | WorkDrive | Drive | Later product, connected over the existing store and HTTP surfaces |
| Documents, spreadsheets, slides | Writer, Sheet, Show | Docs, Sheets, Slides | Later products. Zoho Office Integrator embeds those editors while files stay in the caller's storage |
| Chat | Cliq | Chat | Later product |
| Meetings | Meeting | Meet | Later product |
| Tasks | ToDo | Tasks | Later product on the groupware data that already exists |
| Forms, sites, keep, vault, social | Vault, Connect | Forms, Sites, Keep, Vault | Separate products |

## When the client pass starts

Do not start this pass until shippin.cloud hosts the deployable image.

The first clients are a web mailbox and the same client at phone width. Both use JMAP for mail, CalDAV for calendar, and CardDAV for contacts. Push uses the web-push and email-push capabilities that already exist. This is one client family, not a second mail server.

The control plane is the directory, SCIM, and registry that already exist. It is available only for white-label and enterprise licensing. It is not a Go service, and it is not part of the open mailbox client. The license field stays `deciding` until the license phase. Do not invent a license checker that accepts keys.

After that mail, calendar, and contacts functionality works, documents are a separate product that connects to this server. After documents, photos sync and phone backup are a client on the file nodes that already exist (`urn:ietf:params:jmap:filenode`). They are not a new store and not a drive product inside this phase.
